# Stock Audit Features

## 2. Cycle Counting and ABC Analysis

*Explanation:*
Items are grouped by value or turnover rate into Class A (high value or fast-moving), Class B (medium), and Class C (low value or slow-moving). Instead of shutting down the whole facility for a full stock count, small groups of items are counted on a rotating schedule. Class A items are counted most often and Class C items least often.

*Relevance to an Inventory Management System:*
- Allows continuous auditing without interrupting daily operations.
- Focuses audit effort on the items that matter most financially.
- Detects discrepancies early, before they grow into major losses.
- Improves stock accuracy and helps with better reordering decisions.
